// HEXA Standard Library — cloud/dft_oom_ramfloor_selftest
//
// g5 selftest for the dft-run OOM-preflight RAM-floor fix (handoff 24ab03f0).
//
// BUG: the d11 OOM preflight built DftNodeSpec.total_mem_gib from a FIXED
// DFT_DETACH_RAM_FLOOR (64 GiB) regardless of the pod's actual RAM, so a
// 38-atom Li2MgH16-class cell (~10 GiB/rank) ALWAYS clamped -np to ~6
// (64/10) — renting a 128/384-GiB high-RAM pod gave ZERO extra ranks.
//
// FIX: the rent `--query cpu_ram>=N` value (the floor of the ACTUAL rented
// RAM, pinned into the offer query so the rented node is guaranteed to carry
// it) drives the budget when it exceeds DFT_DETACH_RAM_FLOOR; an absent /
// smaller value falls back to the floor (backward-compatible).
//
// This selftest exercises the budget math directly via the canonical
// tls_dft_mpi_sweet_spot (the REUSED preflight engine) with a node whose
// total_mem_gib is set from the resolved RAM, mirroring _dft_oom_preflight.
// Deterministic — no real pod, no IO.

use "stdlib/cloud/preflight_dft"  // DftSpec · DftNodeSpec · tls_dft_mpi_sweet_spot

